    "title": "'Endless Influx of Immigrants' Has Done 'Significant Damage' to Europe's Social Security Systems: Professor Emeritus",
    "text": "At the United Nations, President Donald Trump took aim at European leadership, accusing them of destroying their own countries through liberal migration policies and aggressive climate agendas. He warned that these strategies are eroding Western economies and cultural foundations. For analysis, NTD spoke to Werner Patzelt, professor emeritus at the Technical University of Dresden.\n'Endless Influx of Immigrants' Has Done 'Significant Damage' to Europe's Social Security Systems: Professor Emeritus\nProfessor emeritus Werner Patzelt discussed President Donald Trump's critique of Europe pushing liberal migration policies and aggressive climate agendas.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 9/25/2025, 12:29:09 AM EDT",
